{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-599f2ce5-f92d-493a-a977-83a6e8c09e75","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b289a2b526d5702","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9003-4apjrlus/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9003-E001.md","content":"# Change default workbench idle culling timeout from 24 hours to 8 hours\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic changes the shipped default for the workbench idle culling timeout\nfrom 24 hours to 8 hours, so that newly installed clusters free GPUs held by\nabandoned workbenches overnight and across weekends without an admin having to\nfind and change the setting. Existing clusters that have an explicitly\nconfigured value are not touched on upgrade. The release note and\ncluster-settings documentation are updated to state the new default and how to\noverride it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Change the shipped default value of the workbench idle culling timeout from\n  24 hours to 8 hours. Culling defaults are administered through the Dashboard\n  (OdhDashboardConfig notebookController settings, backed by the\n  notebook-controller-culler-config ConfigMap); the exact location of the\n  default constant is an implementation detail for the team.\n- Ensure the new default applies to newly installed clusters with no admin\n  configuration required.\n- Ensure upgrade behavior preserves explicitly configured values: clusters\n  where an admin has set the idle culling timeout keep that value.\n- Update the release note and the cluster-settings documentation to state the\n  new 8-hour default and how to override it (incidental documentation\n  touch-up; no new content authored).\n- Validate the passive components that keep working unchanged: the\n  notebook-controller idle culler must stop idle workbenches at the new\n  8-hour default, and the existing Dashboard administration UI must continue\n  to allow overriding the default.\n\nOut of scope: per-project or per-user culling policies, and any changes to\nactivity detection (kernel probe behavior).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a newly installed cluster, when no admin configures the idle culling\n  timeout, then the default idle culling timeout for workbenches is 8 hours.\n- Given a cluster upgraded from a previous release, when the idle culling\n  timeout was explicitly configured by an admin, then that configured value is\n  retained and not reset to the new default.\n- Given a fresh cluster with the new default, when a workbench is left idle\n  past 8 hours, then the notebook-controller culler stops it (passive\n  component validation — culler behavior is unchanged, it consumes the new\n  default).\n- Given the existing Dashboard administration UI, when an admin changes the\n  idle culling timeout, then the override takes effect as before.\n- The release note and cluster-settings documentation state the new 8-hour\n  default and how to override it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P1 | Fully covered — default change plus upgrade-preserving behavior and culler validation. |\n| HLR-2 | P2 | Fully covered — release note and cluster-settings documentation update. |\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25645,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-979e8327c6e9697b","agent_id":"af6137c6cb7e1bb40","session_id":"20ba91d5-262e-4693-852d-b58d21401028","uuid":"f1ebd06e-99b7-4fb9-88cf-240a7fb84aea","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:21:17.274Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9003 into epics"}
